// The continuum hypotheses of continuum_hypothesis, assumed: optional
// assumptions, which a module states it relies on by importing this one.
// Importing continuum_hypothesis gives the statements and the conditional
// proofs between them and assumes none of them. Each axiom assumes its
// statement's body for every universe U < UU0, in next(next(U)). An
// assumption has no computation rule: a result that uses one is listed with
// it and cannot be computable. Implications to excluded middle and choice
// are not claimed here.
import continuum_hypothesis;

// The continuum hypothesis, assumed: CH(U, X, setX, between) refutes a set
// X in next(U) strictly between Nat and PowerSet(U, Nat) in cardinality.
def CH := axiom ContinuumHypothesis;

// The cardinality dichotomy at Nat, assumed: DecidableCH(U, X, setX, above,
// below) merely gives an equivalence of X with Nat or with PowerSet(U, Nat).
// decidable_ch_implies_ch derives CH(U) from it.
def DecidableCH := axiom DecidableContinuumHypothesis;

// The generalized continuum hypothesis, assumed: GCH(U, A, setA, infinite)
// is the continuum hypothesis for a set A in U into which Nat merely
// injects, between A and PowerSet(U, A). gch_implies_ch derives CH(U).
def GCH := axiom GeneralizedContinuumHypothesis;

// The cardinality dichotomy at every infinite set, assumed:
// DecidableGCH(U, A, setA, infinite) is the dichotomy between A and
// PowerSet(U, A). decidable_gch_implies_gch derives GCH(U), and
// decidable_gch_implies_decidable_ch DecidableCH(U).
def DecidableGCH := axiom DecidableGeneralizedContinuumHypothesis;
